# Data
data/

# Secrets / environment
config/scanner/.env
*.env
!config/scanner/default.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# uv
# (uv.lock IS committed for reproducibility)

# Scan corpora under data/ are TRACKED (2026-10-12): a run is a ~45-min scan and
# the corpus every later analysis reads, too expensive to risk losing — so
# data/runs and data/harness are committed. Only the ephemeral scratch namespace
# (dry-run / smoke) stays ignored. Per-row *.env overlays inside a run dir remain
# ignored by the *.env rule above (reproducible from the committed sheet, and that
# rule is a credential-safety backstop — do not weaken it).
data/scratch/
# Transient per-stage run locks (`.lock-<stage>[-<suffix>]`) — released at stage
# end; never corpus. Scoped under data/ so uv.lock stays committed.
data/**/.lock-*

# The targets live in the sibling top-level ../Targets (the tool/targets split);
# their source clones and runtime state are ignored by Targets/.gitignore.

# The other scanners' pinned inputs, together because they are one category:
# the Semgrep ruleset checkout (at the commit pinned in
# semgrep_runner.py — not vendored, for the same reason as a target's
# source clone, and because the rules carry their own licence) and the OSV
# advisory-database snapshot (~230MB of zips, identified by hash in each run's
# metrics rather than by commit).
static-analysis-cache/semgrep-rules/
static-analysis-cache/osv-db/

# Container-managed volumes (bind mounts)
docker/zap-data/
zap-data/

# macOS
.DS_Store
